.TH PORCUPIN 1 "February 2026" "v0.3.3" "Porcupin Manual"
.SH NAME
porcupin \- Headless IPFS backup node for Tezos NFT assets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B porcupin
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B porcupin
is the headless daemon for the Porcupin application. It monitors configured Tezos wallets and automatically pins their associated NFT assets (images, metadata, videos) to an embedded IPFS node.
.PP
When run without options, it starts in daemon mode, continuously syncing and pinning assets.
.SH COMMANDS
Positional subcommands (no leading dash required):
.TP
.B version
Show version banner and exit.
.TP
.B about
Show about information and exit.
.TP
.B settings list
List all current configuration settings.
.TP
.B settings location
Show the config file path.
.TP
.B settings \fIkey\fR
Get the value of a configuration key (dot notation).
.TP
.B settings \fIkey\fR \fIvalue\fR
Set a configuration key to a new value. Dashes and underscores are interchangeable in key names (e.g. backup.max\-concurrency = backup.max_concurrency).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-config \fIpath\fR
Path to configuration file (default: ~/.porcupin/config.yaml).
.TP
.B \-data \fIpath\fR
Data directory for database and IPFS repo (default: ~/.porcupin).
.TP
.B \-version\fR, \fB\-v
Show version banner and exit.
.TP
.B \-about
Show about information and exit.
.SH WALLET MANAGEMENT
.TP
.B \-add\-wallet \fIaddress\fR
Add a Tezos wallet address to track and exit.
.TP
.B \-alias \fIname\fR
Alias for wallet (use with \-\-add\-wallet or \-\-rename\-wallet).
.TP
.B \-rename\-wallet \fIaddress\fR
Rename a wallet (set alias), use with \-\-alias.
.TP
.B \-list\-wallets
List all tracked wallets and exit.
.TP
.B \-remove\-wallet \fIaddress\fR
Remove a wallet address (stop tracking) and exit.
.TP
.B \-unpin\-wallet \fIaddress\fR
Unpin all assets for a wallet and exit.
.TP
.B \-delete\-wallet \fIaddress\fR
Remove wallet and unpin all its assets, then exit.
.SH DAEMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-stats
Show current pinning statistics and exit.
.TP
.B \-retry\-pending
Process all pending assets and exit.
.TP
.B \-gc
Run IPFS garbage collection and exit.
.TP
.B \-update
Check for and install the latest version from GitHub.
.SH API SERVER OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-serve
Start the API server for remote management.
.TP
.B \-api\-port \fIport\fR
Port for the API server (default: 8085). Use with \-\-serve.
.TP
.B \-api\-bind \fIaddress\fR
Bind address for the API server (default: 0.0.0.0). Use with \-\-serve.
.TP
.B \-api\-token \fItoken\fR
Set API token. WARNING: visible in ps output; prefer PORCUPIN_API_TOKEN environment variable.
.TP
.B \-allow\-public
Allow public IP connections. Use with \-\-serve.
.TP
.B \-tls\-cert \fIpath\fR
Path to TLS certificate file. Use with \-\-serve.
.TP
.B \-tls\-key \fIpath\fR
Path to TLS private key file. Use with \-\-serve.
.TP
.B \-regenerate\-token
Regenerate API token and exit.
.SH IPFS OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-ipfs\-port \fIport\fR
IPFS swarm port (default: 4001, 0 = use config value).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PORCUPIN_API_TOKEN
API authentication token (preferred over \-\-api\-token flag).
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the daemon:
.RS
.nf
porcupin
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start with remote API access:
.RS
.nf
porcupin \-\-serve \-\-api\-port 8085
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add a wallet:
.RS
.nf
porcupin \-\-add\-wallet tz1abc... \-\-alias "My Wallet"
.fi
.RE
.PP
View and modify settings:
.RS
.nf
porcupin settings list
porcupin settings backup.max_concurrency
porcupin settings backup.max\-concurrency 2
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run with a custom data directory (systemd):
.RS
.nf
sudo \-u porcupin porcupin \-\-data /var/lib/porcupin \-\-serve
.fi
.RE
.PP
Update to the latest version:
.RS
.nf
porcupin \-\-update
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.porcupin/config.yaml
Configuration file (auto\-created with defaults on first run).
.TP
.I ~/.porcupin/porcupin.db
SQLite database for wallet and asset tracking.
.TP
.I ~/.porcupin/ipfs/
Embedded IPFS repository (pinned content storage).
.SH AUTHOR
Developed by skllzrmy.tez
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ipfs (1)
